Operating margin fell to 19.1% in 2022 from 20.8% in 2021 (a 1.7 percentage‑point decline). The filing attributes that decline mainly to:
- higher raw‑material and logistics costs (management quantifies a ~2.4 percentage‑point negative raw‑material impact), and manufacturing productivity headwinds (including shutdowns and restart effects in Belgium);  
- large litigation/PFAS‑related special items (≈$2.3 billion pre‑tax of net costs for significant litigation in 2022, plus a $0.8 billion Q4 charge related to PFAS exit impairments and a $271 million goodwill impairment) that materially depressed operating results;  
partially offset by pricing, spending discipline and benefits from prior restructuring (management cites ~+1.0 percentage point from organic growth/productivity and other items).

Is operating margin useful here? Yes — it shows overall profitability trends — but the metric must be interpreted with care because 2022 included large, non‑operational special items and a change in segment reporting; 3M therefore presents and discusses both GAAP and “adjusted/ex‑special‑items” margins to better reflect underlying operating performance.
